    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4673051/Central-College/Assistant-Professor-of-Political-Science-Americanist": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science (Americanist)",
      "description": "Central College - Assistant Professor of Political Science (Americanist) In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assistant Professor of Political Science (Americanist) Central College Apply Assistant Professor of Political Science (Americanist) PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Full-time Description Central College seeks applications for a tenure-line, assistant professor of political science in the Behavioral Science Department to begin August 2027. The successful applicant should hold a Ph.D. in Political Science (ABD considered). Our new colleague will join a dynamic and collaborative team of faculty committed to excellence in undergraduate education. The successful candidate will be broadly trained in American politics and teach courses in American government and politics as well as their area(s) of expertise. Specific interest in teaching a course on public policy or regulation is a plus. While a specialization in American Political Institutions is preferred, candidates with a specialization in other American politics subareas are encouraged to apply. Candidates with the ability and an interest in fostering Central’s emerging Model United Nations program are also encouraged to apply. Faculty at Central College also advise and mentor students, assess programs, supervise internships, and engage in scholarship and service that contributes to the institution and the profession. Central College of Pella, Iowa , is a private, four-year liberal arts college with an active student body and a community centered on engaged citizenship. Central is known for its academic rigor, leadership and character formation as outlined in our Mission Statement. Central College is a welcoming learning community committed to vigorous and open inquiry as the best preparation for lives of integrity, creativity, and adaptability. Founded in 1853 and shaped by its Christian heritage, Central College invites learners of all backgrounds and faiths to join us in the pursuit of knowledge, opportunity, and fulfillment. Central participates in NCAA Division III athletics and is a member of the American Rivers Conference. Central’s home is Pella, Iowa , a thriving community of more than 10,000. The community is famous for its annual Tulip Time Festival , its Dutch pastries, unique architecture and its fully functional windmill. Pella is just minutes from Red Rock Lake , Iowa’s largest lake, and is the corporate headquarters of several international companies, including Vermeer Corporation, Pella Corporation, PPI and Lely North America. Central is an active partner with Pella and the Greater Des Moines region. Central College is an equal opportunity employer and a drug/tobacco free workplace. Academic positions at Central College use E-Verify. To be eligible for this position, applicant must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction. Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. Requirements Application Requirements: Review of applications will begin January 4, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. Candidates recommended for employment are subject to a background check. Please submit the required following materials online: a letter of application relating your qualifications to the position and the College an updated curriculum vita copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a statement of teaching philosophy contact information for three references who are willing to submit confidential letters of reference addressing the candidate’s qualifications Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4676099/Central-College/Assistant-Professor-of-Political-Science-Comparative-Politics-or-International-Relations": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science (Comparative Politics or International Relations)",
      "description": "Central College - Assistant Professor of Political Science (Comparative Politics or International Relations) In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assistant Professor of Political Science (Comparative Politics or International Relations) Central College Apply Assistant Professor of Political Science (Comparative Politics or International Relations) PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Full-time Description Central College seeks applications for a tenure-line, assistant professor of political science in the Behavioral Science Department to begin August 2027. The successful applicant should hold a Ph.D. in Political Science (ABD considered). Our new colleague will join a dynamic and collaborative team of faculty committed to excellence in undergraduate education. The successful candidate will be broadly trained in either comparative politics or international relations and will be expected to teach introductory-level courses in comparative politics or international relations in additional to upper-level courses in candidate’s area of expertise. Specific interest in teaching a course on immigration is a plus. While a regional specialization in Latin America is preferred, candidates with a regional specialization in other areas of the world are encouraged to apply. Candidates with the ability and an interest in fostering Central’s emerging Model United Nations program are also encouraged to apply. Faculty at Central College also advise and mentor students, assess programs, supervise internships, and engage in scholarship and service that contributes to the institution and the profession. Central College of Pella, Iowa , is a private, four-year liberal arts college with an active student body and a community centered on engaged citizenship. Central is known for its academic rigor, leadership and character formation as outlined in our Mission Statement.  Central College is a welcoming learning community committed to vigorous and open inquiry as the best preparation for lives of integrity, creativity, and adaptability. Founded in 1853 and shaped by its Christian heritage, Central College invites learners of all backgrounds and faiths to join us in the pursuit of knowledge, opportunity, and fulfillment.  Central participates in NCAA Division III athletics and is a member of the American Rivers Conference. Central’s home is Pella, Iowa, a thriving community of more than 10,000. The community is famous for its annual Tulip Time Festival , its Dutch pastries, unique architecture and its fully functional windmill. Pella is just minutes from Red Rock Lake , Iowa’s largest lake, and is the corporate headquarters of several international companies, including Vermeer Corporation, Pella Corporation, PPI and Lely North America.  Central is an active partner with Pella and the Greater Des Moines region . Central College is an equal opportunity employer and a drug/tobacco free workplace. Academic positions at Central College use E-Verify. To be eligible for this position, applicant must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction. Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. Requirements Application Requirements: Review of applications will begin January 4, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. Candidates recommended for employment are subject to a background check. Please submit the following materials online: a letter of application relating your qualifications to the position and the College an updated curriculum vita copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a statement of teaching philosophy a list of three confidential references with contact information who are willing to submit a letter of reference addressing the candidate’s qualifications Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4684951/Central-College/Bus-Driver": {
      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Central College - Bus Driver In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Bus Driver Central College Apply Bus Driver PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Part-time Description Serve as college bus driver for various purposes including transporting students to athletic events, to and from airport, train and/or bus station, etc. Follow the time schedule assigned by the Central College Athletics Department or the activity sponsor. Exhibit sound judgment in following safe driving standards; monitor vehicle operation safety (i.e. tire pressure, brakes, lights, wipers, oil and fuel levels, etc.). Serve as a role model for the mission of Central College. Must enjoy being around people and have a willingness to accommodate a wide constituent pool as the position may require driving board members and college guests in addition to students. Requirements High School graduate or GED and 2 years’ experience as a driver CDL with Passenger Endorsement is Required Medical Certificate (in accordance with the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Regulations) Confirmed negative pre-employment drug test Must have a safe driving record Good knowledge of Iowa Driver’s Manual and DOT’s A Motor Carrier’s Guide to Improving Highway Safety Ability to communicate effectively and exercise good human relations skills in establishing and maintaining effective working relations with the college community Compliance with all applicable DOT regulations, including submission to drug and alcohol testing Candidates are also subject to a background check Must be willing and available for evening and weekend work Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4690197/Central-College/Assistant-Professor-or-Lecturer-in-Organizational-Communication": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Lecturer in Organizational Communication",
      "description": "Central College - Assistant Professor or Lecturer in Organizational Communication In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assistant Professor or Lecturer in Organizational Communication Central College Apply Assistant Professor or Lecturer in Organizational Communication PELLA, IA Apply Job Type Full-time Description Central College seeks applications for a tenure-line, assistant professor or nontenure-line lecturer of communication studies in the Business and Communication Studies Department beginning August 2027. The successful applicant should hold a Ph.D.  (ABD considered) in communication studies for the appointment to assistant professor, or a master’s degree for the lecturer appointment. Our new colleague will join a dynamic and collaborative team of faculty committed to excellence in undergraduate education. The successful candidate will be broadly trained in communication studies and have an appreciation for the liberal arts environment. Primary teaching responsibilities include organizational communication, business and professional communication, introductory communication classes, or courses in the candidate’s area of specialty. In addition, the successful candidate will be able to teach in the College’s first-year or second-year interdisciplinary seminar. Faculty at Central College also advise and mentor students, assess programs, supervise internships, and engage in scholarship and service that contributes to the institution and the profession. The Communication Studies program, as part of the Business and Communication Studies Department, provides students with a broad-based curriculum through a combination of theoretical grounding and applied experience in an effort to cultivate critical thinking, clear writing, articulate speaking and proficiency with digital media. Our students study communication within a variety of contexts, particularly those related to media citizenship, civic responsibility, professional engagement, and personal relationships. The faculty in the department and across the Central campus interact in an academically stimulating and congenial environment with a focus on student success. Central College of Pella, Iowa, is a private, four-year liberal arts college with an active student body and a community centered on engaged citizenship. Central is known for its academic rigor, leadership and character formation as outlined in our Mission Statement.  Central College is a welcoming learning community committed to vigorous and open inquiry as the best preparation for lives of integrity, creativity, and adaptability. Founded in 1853 and shaped by its Christian heritage, Central College invites learners of all backgrounds and faiths to join us in the pursuit of knowledge, opportunity, and fulfillment.  Central participates in NCAA Division III athletics and is a member of the American Rivers Conference. Central’s home is Pella, Iowa , a thriving community of more than 10,000. The community is famous for its annual Tulip Time Festival , its Dutch pastries, unique architecture and its fully functional windmill. Pella is just minutes from Red Rock Lake , Iowa’s largest lake, and is the corporate headquarters of several international companies, including Vermeer Corporation, Pella Corporation, PPI and Lely North America. Central is an active partner with Pella and the Greater Des Moines region. Central College is an equal opportunity employer and a drug/tobacco free workplace. Academic positions at Central College use E-Verify. To be eligible for this position, applicant must be legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction. Applicants who now or may in the future require visa sponsorship to work in the United States are not eligible. Requirements Application Requirements: Review of applications will begin January 12, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. Candidates recommended for employment are subject to a background check. Please submit the required following materials online: a letter of application relating your qualifications to the position and the College an updated curriculum vita copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a statement of teaching philosophy contact information for three references who are willing to submit confidential letters of reference addressing the candidate’s qualifications Apply View All Jobs Powered by Paylocity Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy SMS Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy"
    }
  },
